{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And he rose early.</b> He bestirred himself for the command (Pesachim 4)." "<b>And he saddled.</b> He himself — and did not order one of his servants, for love disrupts the routine." "<b>His two young men.</b> Ishmael and Eliezer, for a person of consequence may not set out on the road without two men (Bereshit Rabbah), so that if one needs to relieve himself and steps away, the second will be with him." "<b>And he split.</b> Targum: וְצַלַּח, as in ״וְצָלְחוּ הַיַּרְדֵּן״ (II Samuel 19) — a term of splitting; פינדר״א בְּלַעַ״ז."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {3 "the la'az is Old French fendre, 'to split/cleave'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:53.336113642Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}